  "notes": [
    "**Robar** is a regular -AR verb",
    "No stem changes in any tense",
    "Follows the same pattern as regular -AR verbs like hablar, trabajar",
    "Past participle: robado (robbed/stolen)",
    "Most common and natural word for stealing/robbing in Argentina and all of Latin America",
    "Common usage: *robar un banco* (to rob a bank), *robar el tren* (to rob the train), *me robaron* (they robbed me), *robar dinero* (to steal money)",
    "Related words: *ladrón/ladrona* (thief), *robo* (robbery/theft)"
